 {
  "id": "N12",
  "user": "Michael Turner",
  "question": "Compare downtime of WELL-0001, WELL-0005 and WELL-0121 in 2026 as a bar chart.",
  "answer": "**WELL-0001 was down 21 days** (1 Jan 2026\u201316 Oct 2026), from 3 weekly inspections where it was not producing oil:\n- 7 May 2026 (INS-0001-0181): wellhead 30.8 \u00b0C vs air 29.2 \u00b0C, only 1.6 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Flowline corrosion pinhole leak (MNT-0001-028); Pump jack counterweights rebalanced. Expect slightly lower wellhead temperature (~3 C) from now on; this is normal. (CTX-0001-002).\n- 8 Oct 2026 (INS-0001-0202): wellhead 23.4 \u00b0C vs air 20.2 \u00b0C, only 3.2 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Flowline leak causing spill (MNT-0001-032); Pump jack counterweights rebalanced. Expect slightly lower wellhead temperature (~3 C) from now on; this is normal. (CTX-0001-002); Well shut in from 7 Oct for planned rod string replacement. Work order not yet in the maintenance system. Expected back online around 20 Oct. (CTX-0001-003).\n- 15 Oct 2026 (INS-0001-0203): wellhead 25.6 \u00b0C vs air 22.4 \u00b0C, only 3.2 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Pump jack counterweights rebalanced. Expect slightly lower wellhead temperature (~3 C) from now on; this is normal. (CTX-0001-002); Well shut in from 7 Oct for planned rod string replacement. Work order not yet in the maintenance system. Expected back online around 20 Oct. (CTX-0001-003).\n**WELL-0005 was down 42 days** (1 Jan 2026\u201316 Oct 2026), from 6 weekly inspections where it was not producing oil:\n- 18 Jun 2026 (INS-0005-0188): wellhead 42.0 \u00b0C vs air 33.9 \u00b0C, only 8.1 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0005-031).\n- 25 Jun 2026 (INS-0005-0189): wellhead 46.8 \u00b0C vs air 39.0 \u00b0C, only 7.8 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0005-031).\n- 2 Jul 2026 (INS-0005-0190): wellhead 47.8 \u00b0C vs air 38.0 \u00b0C, only 9.8 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0005-031).\n- 9 Jul 2026 (INS-0005-0191): wellhead 45.1 \u00b0C vs air 34.8 \u00b0C, only 10.3 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0005-031).\n- 16 Jul 2026 (INS-0005-0192): wellhead 50.3 \u00b0C vs air 39.5 \u00b0C, only 10.8 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0005-031); Scheduled wellhead valve service (MNT-0005-032).\n- 23 Jul 2026 (INS-0005-0193): wellhead 36.4 \u00b0C vs air 34.4 \u00b0C, only 2.0 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0005-031).\n**WELL-0121 was down 70 days** (1 Jan 2026\u201316 Oct 2026), from 10 weekly inspections where it was not producing oil:\n- 28 May 2026 (INS-0121-0186): wellhead 34.9 \u00b0C vs air 35.2 \u00b0C, only -0.3 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Gearbox oil leak (MNT-0121-031).\n- 4 Jun 2026 (INS-0121-0187): wellhead 32.0 \u00b0C vs air 32.0 \u00b0C, only 0.0 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Gearbox oil leak (MNT-0121-031).\n- 11 Jun 2026 (INS-0121-0188): wellhead 35.4 \u00b0C vs air 32.0 \u00b0C, only 3.4 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Gearbox oil leak (MNT-0121-031).\n- 18 Jun 2026 (INS-0121-0189): wellhead 33.3 \u00b0C vs air 32.9 \u00b0C, only 0.4 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Gearbox oil leak (MNT-0121-031).\n- 3 Sep 2026 (INS-0121-0200): wellhead 29.8 \u00b0C vs air 29.2 \u00b0C, only 0.6 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Scheduled wellhead valve service (MNT-0121-033); Prime mover failure (MNT-0121-034).\n- 10 Sep 2026 (INS-0121-0201): wellhead 34.4 \u00b0C vs air 29.5 \u00b0C, only 4.9 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0121-034).\n- 17 Sep 2026 (INS-0121-0202): wellhead 27.1 \u00b0C vs air 27.9 \u00b0C, only -0.8 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0121-034).\n- 24 Sep 2026 (INS-0121-0203): wellhead 33.0 \u00b0C vs air 27.8 \u00b0C, only 5.2 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0121-034).\n- 8 Oct 2026 (INS-0121-0205): wellhead 29.0 \u00b0C vs air 25.5 \u00b0C, only 3.5 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0121-035).\n- 15 Oct 2026 (INS-0121-0206): wellhead 22.7 \u00b0C vs air 21.7 \u00b0C, only 1.0 \u00b0C warmer. Cause: Prime mover failure (MNT-0121-035).\n\nDowntime = 7 days per non-producing weekly inspection (Dataset Guide).",
